cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference Threadline in academic or published work, please cite it as below."
title: "Threadline: a real-time collaboration platform built across three independently deployable services"
abstract: >-
  Threadline is a room-centered collaboration workspace in which a room is
  simultaneously a live session (WebRTC video, audio, screen share, whiteboard,
  chat, shared editor) and the durable record of what happened in it. It is
  built as three independently deployable services that deliberately do not
  trust each other's enforcement: a Next.js web tier, an Express API tier
  owning identity and attribute-based access control, and a Cloudflare Durable
  Object per room owning presence and WebRTC signalling. Every trust boundary
  re-performs its own authorization check rather than inheriting an upstream
  one.
type: software
